Day 10 — AWS Security, IAM & Compliance Architecture

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your organization has multiple AWS accounts and teams. How will you design IAM for least privilege and scalability?

2️⃣ A leaked IAM access key was found in a public repository. What immediate and long-term actions will you take?

3️⃣ Developers need temporary access to AWS resources without long-lived credentials. How will you design this securely?

4️⃣ You want to restrict AWS usage to specific regions only. How will you enforce this at scale?

5️⃣ An application running on EC2 needs access to S3 and DynamoDB securely. How will you configure IAM roles?

6️⃣ You must ensure all data at rest is encrypted using customer-managed keys. How will you enforce this?

7️⃣ A security audit requires visibility into all IAM changes. How will you enable tracking and alerts?

8️⃣ You want to protect applications from common web attacks like SQL injection and XSS. Which AWS services will you use?

9️⃣ An internal API should be accessible only from private networks. How will you design network-level security?

🔟 You need automatic detection of compromised instances or suspicious activity. How will you design this?

1️⃣1️⃣ Cross-account access is required between prod and shared services accounts. How will you configure trust securely?

1️⃣2️⃣ You want to prevent accidental deletion of critical resources. How will you implement guardrails?

1️⃣3️⃣ Secrets are currently stored in plain text environment variables. How will you redesign secrets management?

1️⃣4️⃣ Compliance requires periodic key rotation and access reviews. How will you automate this?

1️⃣5️⃣ A zero-trust security model is mandated. How will you apply this across IAM, network, and services?

